              '../../videos/clip1.mp4',       
              '../../images/clinic1.jpg',     
              '../../videos/clip2.mp4'        
          ]
      };
  </script>
  <div id="banner-placeholder"></div>

  <article class="post-article reveal reveal-1">
    
    <header class="post-header">
      <div class="post-meta">
        <span>August 15th, 2026</span>
        <span class="post-category">Progress Note</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="post-title">Finally, Hello World</h1>
      <p class="post-intro">It's been a long journey, but I finally built my website from the ground up.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p>I’ve tried multiple website builders for my blogs and websites in the past. The only one that really appealed to me was Squarespace, mainly because of its clean UI. But I was never truly comfortable using a service without knowing what was going on under the hood. There were so many times I wanted to push a design element just a bit further, but Squarespace limited the way I wanted to design.</p>
      
      <p>I had a basic understanding of HTML and CSS, but nowhere near enough to build a website from scratch. It was frustrating. I didn't want to go back to Wix (too laggy) or WordPress (outdated UI).</p>
      
      <p>Then… I had the idea to use AI to help me build a website… and here I am! I used Gemini Pro to help me pull this off.</p>
      
      <p>This has been quite a journey. I had to make a lot of decisions along the way, and it wasn't an easy job—figuring out the folder structure, file structure, code structure, hosting services, designs, fonts, and more.</p>
      
      <p>I am so ready to share everything. I plan to use this personal journal as my diary.</p>
      
      <p>I hope you guys enjoy it.</p>
      
      <p>BYE!</p>
    </div>

    <footer class="post-footer">
      <a href="../personal-journal.html" class="back-link">← Back to Personal Journal</a>
      <a href="#" class="next-link">Next Entry →</a>
    </footer>
  </article>

  <div id="site-footer-placeholder"></div>

  <div id="footer-placeholder"></div>

